{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnCriterion","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridgeTwo","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionsOfBridge"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.spechtProduct_bijective_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.spechtProduct_bijective_le12","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnLe12.lean#L106-L113","doc":"The bijectivity statement behind `spechtEquiv_le12`, for callers that want the map rather than\nthe equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.spechtEquiv_le12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.spechtEquiv_le12","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnLe12.lean#L87-L104","doc":"**The Wedderburn split of `k[S_n]`, unconditionally, for `n ≤ 12`.**\n\n`k[S_n] ≃ₐ[k] ∏_{μ ⊢ n} End_k(S^μ)` over any characteristic-zero field: partition-indexed, block\n`μ` acting on the Specht module `S^μ`.\n\nEverything the split needs is proved — the commutant is the base field (W2), the map is\npartition-indexed and block-sized by construction, and it is injective — leaving only the count\n`Σ_μ (#SYT μ)² = n!`, which the corpus proves for `n ≤ 12` with no RSK correspondence\n(`PartitionsOfBridge.rskBurnsideHolds_le12`).\n\n`-- Ref: [sagan2001] §1.10, §2.4; [james1984representation]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.sum_numSYT_sq_of_rskBurnside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.sum_numSYT_sq_of_rskBurnside","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnLe12.lean#L79-L85","doc":"**Reindexing the RSK/Burnside identity** from `Nat.Partition n` onto `PartitionIndex n`, which\nis the index the Specht machinery uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.numSYT_partitionEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.numSYT_partitionEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnLe12.lean#L72-L77","doc":"`#SYT` in the `BraidKnot` (0-indexed) encoding agrees with `dimSYT`, which is stated in the\n`Mathlib` (1-indexed) encoding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.diagram_partitionEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtWedderburnLe12.diagram_partitionEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtWedderburnLe12.lean#L66-L70","doc":"The diagram attached to a partition by `partitionEquivYoungIndex` is the one\n`RSKBurnsideTarget.partitionShape` names: both are `ofRowLens` of the weakly-decreasingly sorted\nparts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}